  "awb---integration-feature-1": "<h3>Knife 301 is spot 1 on the waitlist</h3><p>Tavish Forge hammers out one run of 300 chef's knives at $145 each, and the form says the run ships the week of Jan 11. Every order after 300 goes to the waitlist for the next run. Winnifred Mabe places order 301 and becomes spot 1.</p>",
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Pre-Order Form Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a pre order form?\", \"a\": \"A pre order form takes orders for an item before it is made or in stock. It records who ordered what, and when each order will be ready. The seller then makes or buys stock against those totals.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I create a pre-order form?\", \"a\": \"List your items, the most you can make of each, and the date each one is ready. Describe that in one prompt to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a>, and it returns a working form that stops selling each item at its limit and takes no orders after the last day you set.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a pre order form template include?\", \"a\": \"A pre order form template should include the buyer's contact details, each item with its price and a quantity box, the ready or ship date, and pickup or shipping details. Add a limit per item and a closing date. If you also keep a pre order form PDF at the counter for walk-in buyers, enter those orders into the same list to keep the counts right.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I make a free pre order form for a small business?\", \"a\": \"To make a free pre order form, start on Emergent's free tier. The free tier covers building and publishing. Describe your items, prices, limits, and ready dates in one prompt. Forms built with Emergent have no response caps, and a busy launch week never closes the form early. A school or team collecting sizes before a season can build a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/uniform-order'>uniform order form</a> the same way.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I make a pre-order form stop taking orders when an item sells out?\", \"a\": \"Set a limit on each item, and the form closes that item once submitted orders reach it. Count units, not orders: a buyer who takes 3 uses 3 of the limit. Then choose what a late buyer sees, such as a sold-out label, a date for the next batch, or a waitlist.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should I do when orders from a pre-order form cannot ship on the promised date?\", \"a\": \"Tell each buyer before the date passes and ask whether they will wait. For most goods a customer orders by mail, telephone, fax, or on the Internet, the FTC's mail order rule says a seller who can ship later must seek the customer's consent to the delay. A seller who cannot ship must promptly cancel the order and make a full refund.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do I turn pre-order form orders into a production plan?\", \"a\": \"Add up what each item needs for each ready date, then work back from the earliest date to set what gets made each day. Every order sits in a database you own, and a dashboard on that table shows the daily list. Some pre-orders end in a visit, such as installing shelving a buyer ordered; schedule that visit on a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/work-order'>work order form</a>.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do customers choose a pickup time on a pre-order form?\", \"a\": \"Buyers pick from a list of pickup slots, each with its own limit, and a full slot drops off the list. Size each slot by how many orders your counter can hand out in that time. Repeat the slot and the pickup address in the confirmation email.\"}, {\"q\": \"When should a pre-order form close?\", \"a\": \"Close it early enough to buy supplies and make everything before the ready date. Work back from that date: production time, plus the lead time on supplies, plus a day of slack. Set two closing rules on pre order forms with a fixed run, the date and the limit, and stop at whichever comes first.\"}, {\"q\": \"Can one pre-order form handle sizes and colors?\", \"a\": \"Yes. Give each item a size and a color choice, and set the limit per variant when each one runs out on its own, such as 40 mediums and 20 larges. In a form built with Emergent, you add a size or a color later by prompting. For shirts ordered in a size grid, a <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder/t-shirt-order'>t shirt order form</a> with a quantity per size is a closer fit.\"}]}; </script></div></div>",
  "afb---prompt": "<p>Build a pre order form that saves every response to a database I own.</p><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbPrompt = {\"default\": \"Build a pre order form that saves every response to a database I own.\", \"chips\": [{\"label\": \"Pickup Time Slots\", \"add\": \"Add pickup time slots that each hold a set number of orders.\"}, {\"label\": \"Order Limits\", \"add\": \"Add order limits that close each item when it sells out.\"}, {\"label\": \"Waitlist\", \"add\": \"Add a waitlist that takes orders after an item sells out.\"}, {\"label\": \"Pickup Reminders\", \"add\": \"Add pickup reminders that email each buyer before pickup day.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
